{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>So shall he sprinkle, etc.</b> The meaning is like 'he shall be exalted and lifted up' [Isaiah 52:13]. Just as it was true that his appearance was marred before the eyes of those who saw, so a time will come when he will take vengeance upon them." "And the meaning of <b>he shall sprinkle:</b> He will spill their blood." "<b>Then kings shall shut their mouths.</b> And 'over him' is like 'for his sake'." "<b>That which was not told them, they saw.</b> That it never entered the hearts of the nations that there would be salvation for Israel."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 52, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:15.365164038Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}